#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:5
msgid "AMD HSMP interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:7
msgid ""
"Newer Fam19h(model 0x00-0x1f, 0x30-0x3f, 0x90-0x9f, 0xa0-0xaf), Fam1Ah(model "
"0x00-0x1f) EPYC server line of processors from AMD support system management "
"functionality via HSMP (Host System Management Port)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:11
msgid ""
"The Host System Management Port (HSMP) is an interface to provide OS-level "
"software with access to system management functions via a set of mailbox "
"registers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:15
msgid ""
"More details on the interface can be found in chapter \"7 Host System "
"Management Port (HSMP)\" of the family/model PPR Eg: https://docs.amd.com/v/"
"u/en-US/55898_B1_pub_0_50"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:20
msgid ""
"HSMP interface is supported on EPYC line of server CPUs and MI300A (APU)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:24
msgid "HSMP device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:26
msgid ""
"amd_hsmp driver under drivers/platforms/x86/amd/hsmp/ has separate driver "
"files for ACPI object based probing, platform device based probing and for "
"the common code for these two drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:30
msgid ""
"Kconfig option CONFIG_AMD_HSMP_PLAT compiles plat.c and creates amd_hsmp.ko. "
"Kconfig option CONFIG_AMD_HSMP_ACPI compiles acpi.c and creates hsmp_acpi."
"ko. Selecting any of these two configs automatically selects "
"CONFIG_AMD_HSMP. This compiles common code hsmp.c and creates hsmp_common.ko "
"module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:35
msgid ""
"Both the ACPI and plat drivers create the miscdevice /dev/hsmp to let user "
"space programs run hsmp mailbox commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:38
msgid "The ACPI object format supported by the driver is defined below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:40
msgid ""
"$ ls -al /dev/hsmp crw-r--r-- 1 root root 10, 123 Jan 21 21:41 /dev/hsmp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:43
msgid "Characteristics of the dev node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:44
msgid "Write mode is used for running set/configure commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:45
msgid "Read mode is used for running get/status monitor commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:47
msgid "Access restrictions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:48
msgid "Only root user is allowed to open the file in write mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:49
msgid "The file can be opened in read mode by all the users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:51
msgid "In-kernel integration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:52
msgid ""
"Other subsystems in the kernel can use the exported transport function "
"hsmp_send_message()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:54
msgid "Locking across callers is taken care by the driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:58
msgid "HSMP sysfs interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:60
msgid "Metrics table binary sysfs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:62
msgid ""
"AMD MI300A MCM provides GET_METRICS_TABLE message to retrieve most of the "
"system management information from SMU in one go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:65
msgid ""
"The metrics table is made available as hexadecimal sysfs binary file under "
"per socket sysfs directory created at /sys/devices/platform/amd_hsmp/"
"socket%d/metrics_bin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:69
msgid "Note: lseek() is not supported as entire metrics table is read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:71
msgid ""
"The sysfs metrics_bin path supports only HSMP protocol version 6 and, "
"because it is a file read, can return a torn snapshot if userspace reads in "
"pieces.  The protocol version 7 metric table (~13 KB) also exceeds "
"PAGE_SIZE, so a read returns ``-EOPNOTSUPP`` there.  For atomic reads on any "
"protocol version, use the ``HSMP_IOCTL_GET_TELEMETRY_DATA`` ioctl on /dev/"
"hsmp (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:78
msgid ""
"Metrics table definitions will be documented as part of Public PPR. The same "
"is defined in the amd_hsmp.h header."
msgstr ""

